{% extends "_base.j2" %}
{% block main %}
<span class="eyebrow">Learn · Real-node observability</span>
<h1>Measurements</h1>
<p class="lede">Measurements are reusable taps that attach to a version-pinned real-node scenario. They explain node and protocol behavior without replacing the security workload or turning DWARF into a simulator.</p>

<p class="definition-actions"><a class="cta cta--primary" href="/operate/measurements">Browse measurements</a><a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/operate/measurement-profiles">Browse profiles</a></p>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="definitions">
  <span class="eyebrow">Model</span>
  <h2>Tap, profile, scenario, evidence</h2>
  <div class="tile-grid">
    <article class="tile"><span class="tile__eyebrow">Measurement</span><span class="tile__metric tile__metric--label">one named signal</span><span class="tile__sub">Defines compatibility, source, collector lifecycle, units, correlation IDs, artifacts, and optional threshold behavior.</span></article>
    <article class="tile"><span class="tile__eyebrow">Measurement profile</span><span class="tile__metric tile__metric--label">reusable selection</span><span class="tile__sub">Groups compatible taps for one implementation and target mode. Scenarios may override or explicitly disable them.</span></article>
    <article class="tile"><span class="tile__eyebrow">Run evidence</span><span class="tile__metric tile__metric--label">retained, not inferred</span><span class="tile__sub">Collector state, raw input, normalized events, distributions, reasons for unavailable data, target identity, and reports stay in the run bundle.</span></article>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="modes">
  <span class="eyebrow">Target modes</span>
  <h2>Use the least intrusive truthful source</h2>
  <div class="version-catalog">
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>stock</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">preferred</span></div><p>Existing node traces, metrics, real wire observations, and external process/container counters. No node source modification.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>coverage</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--unknown">execution proof</span></div><p>Revision-qualified compiler coverage proves production code paths were reached. Coverage is not a latency source and does not itself prove a security property.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>patched</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--unknown">selective</span></div><p>Revision-locked node instrumentation supplies internal boundaries stock telemetry cannot expose. Claims require exact build provenance plus a matching stock control and overhead calibration.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="interpretation">
  <span class="eyebrow">Interpretation</span>
  <h2>Every terminal outcome keeps its time</h2>
  <p>Accepted, rejected, invalid, duplicate, timed-out, disconnected, and unclassified attempts remain in the combined timing population and in per-outcome distributions. A missing boundary is <code>unavailable</code>, never zero. Resource counters identify whether they describe the node process, its network namespace/container, or the DWARF controller.</p>
  <p>Raw integer nanoseconds are retained when a revision-locked tap supplies them. Collectors prefer that field and derive fractional microseconds without removing the sub-microsecond part. The existing integer microsecond field remains for compatibility, and legacy whole-microsecond evidence remains readable. Measurement revisions are additive: Card 03 keeps <code>whole-microseconds-v1</code>; current Cards 01, 02, and 05 use <code>nanoseconds-v2</code>; Card 04 uses Amaru <code>nanoseconds-v3</code> and Cardano-node <code>nanoseconds-v2</code>.</p>
  <p>Measurements do not change the security verdict by default. A scenario fails because its security assertion failed; a collector error is shown separately. Threshold gating is available only when explicitly enabled.</p>
  <p>A completed run can contain a security finding. Completed means that DWARF finished the run and retained the evidence. It does not mean that the target passed. The failed assertion and its <code>fail</code> verdict remain visible.</p>
</section>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="reports">
  <span class="eyebrow">Run result</span>
  <h2>What the browser and bundle retain</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>measurements/selection.json</code> — exact profile, tap definitions, compatibility, target identity, collector states, and gate policy.</li>
    <li><code>measurements/report.json</code> and <code>report.md</code> — point values, counts, distributions, throughput, resource cost, and unavailable reasons.</li>
    <li><code>measurements/collectors/&lt;id&gt;/</code> — collector-specific normalized data, samples, correlations, and raw evidence.</li>
    <li>The run inspector — compact status, exact node identity, collector errors, searchable metrics, per-outcome distributions, and downloads.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="implementation-status">
  <span class="eyebrow">Current proof status</span>
  <h2>Amaru and Cardano-node are independently proven end to end</h2>
  <div class="version-catalog">
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>Amaru 10.11.20260912</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">GUI proven</span></div><p><a href="/operate/runs/20260918T234213Z-64959688"><code>20260918T234213Z-64959688</code></a> retained 100 timed hostile attempts, real protocol and block-application samples, independent sync progress, real target resources, exact source/image identity, 11 finalized collectors, and zero collector errors.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>Amaru patched boundary</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">paired proof</span></div><p><a href="/operate/runs/20260919T135417Z-cca4cc8d"><code>20260919T135417Z-cca4cc8d</code></a> proved the revision-locked Handshake instrumentation with exact internal count parity. Matched stock run <a href="/operate/runs/20260919T142302Z-f856f303"><code>20260919T142302Z-f856f303</code></a> used the identical 120-attempt workload and terminal outcomes.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>Cardano-node 11.1.2</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">GUI proven</span></div><p><a href="/operate/runs/20260919T032200Z-59f94558"><code>20260919T032200Z-59f94558</code></a> retained 100 timed hostile attempts, accepted and rejected Plutus transactions, stock and patched protocol/block/epoch/VM signals, real target resources, exact build identity, all 12 collectors finalized, and zero collector errors.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>Mixed comparison</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--unknown">deferred</span></div><p>Mixed-node measurement comparison has not started. Both independent workflows are proven, but a mixed comparison remains deferred and requires a separate contract.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Observer-overhead envelope:</strong> the paired Amaru calibration uses a 5% maximum absolute delta across mean, median, p95, and p99, with at least 30 samples per leg and exact identity, workload, runner, timing, hardware, and outcome parity. The largest observed delta was <code>0.059686888%</code> across 120 stock and 120 patched samples, so the common externally observed Handshake round trip was within the envelope. This check is informational and non-gating. It does not bound internal hook cost, throughput, saturation, or another workload.</p>
  <p>The retained Amaru devnet uses <code>system_start: 0</code>. Its raw node-reported slot-start age is therefore retained for audit but excluded from comparable propagation-latency claims. Cardano patched values remain revision-specific and require their paired stock control before they are used as performance authority.</p>
</section>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="five-client-examples">
  <span class="eyebrow">Final retained examples</span>
  <h2>The five frozen cards are complete</h2>
  <p>The accepted labels are <code>framework proven</code>, <code>collection proven</code>, and <code>client requirement complete</code>. Each card has a separate Amaru execution and Cardano-node execution. These runs are not a mixed-node benchmark.</p>
  <div class="version-catalog">
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>01 · CBOR decoding</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">complete</span></div><p>Fixed Amaru revision <code>d3a6dafcced78f5809a96619e883cf04911d2bdc</code> run <a href="/operate/runs/20260920T235440Z-050046a4"><code>20260920T235440Z-050046a4</code></a> and Cardano-node run <a href="/operate/runs/20260920T132629Z-ea000d37"><code>20260920T132629Z-ea000d37</code></a> pass the frozen corpus. The old Amaru failure remains a completed security finding.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>02 · Plutus VM</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">complete</span></div><p>Additive on-chain Plutus V2 Amaru run <a href="/operate/runs/20260921T013953Z-565b77c3"><code>20260921T013953Z-565b77c3</code></a> and Cardano-node run <a href="/operate/runs/20260920T135958Z-362eedc7"><code>20260920T135958Z-362eedc7</code></a> retain evaluator results, budgets, real transaction outcomes, and chain progress.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>03 · Invalid mini-protocol</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">complete</span></div><p>Amaru run <a href="/operate/runs/20260920T072858Z-2cc3bb0c"><code>20260920T072858Z-2cc3bb0c</code></a> and Cardano-node run <a href="/operate/runs/20260920T073447Z-ab81bfb7"><code>20260920T073447Z-ab81bfb7</code></a> preserve the accepted <code>whole-microseconds-v1</code> evidence.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>04 · Block application</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">complete</span></div><p>Amaru canonical-progress run <a href="/operate/runs/20260921T035546Z-9747122c"><code>20260921T035546Z-9747122c</code></a> and Cardano-node run <a href="/operate/runs/20260921T021935Z-3b58eafc"><code>20260921T021935Z-3b58eafc</code></a> retain canonical progress, raw fork evidence, correlations, and exact timing.</p></article>
    <article class="version-card"><div class="version-card__head"><h3>05 · Restart and sync</h3><span class="version-badge version-badge--confirmed">complete</span></div><p>Amaru run <a href="/operate/runs/20260921T045619Z-15e864a0"><code>20260921T045619Z-15e864a0</code></a> and Cardano-node run <a href="/operate/runs/20260921T045807Z-8e2bbb0e"><code>20260921T045807Z-8e2bbb0e</code></a> retain ordered readiness gates, controlled sync ranges, health, and restart-window resources.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Child explanation:</strong> DWARF finished five careful recipes with each node. It kept the old problems in the record, and it kept the new proof that passes.</p>
</section>

<hr class="hairline">

<section id="troubleshooting">
  <span class="eyebrow">Troubleshooting</span>
  <h2>Read absence honestly</h2>
  <dl class="definition-summary">
    <div><dt>incompatible</dt><dd>The tap does not support the resolved implementation, version, mode, or capability set. Explicit incompatible selections stop before workload execution.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>unavailable</dt><dd>The collector ran but the bounded workload did not expose enough evidence for that boundary. Inspect the retained reason and source artifact.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>collector error</dt><dd>The optional tap failed to prepare, start, stop, or finalize. The error remains visible and non-gating unless an explicit threshold gate says otherwise.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>patched-only value</dt><dd>Do not treat it as a production-node performance claim until the paired stock workload and observer-overhead calibration are retained.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>
{% endblock %}
